<mxCell id="stg" value="STAGE SUMMARY — HUB ↔ each Spoke over HA VPN (IPsec) with Cloud Router BGP on both ends; Hub Cloud DNS + per-spoke Cloud DNS joined by DNS peering.&#10;1 — User logs in to the WebApp (session + JWT).   2 — User clicks &quot;Open Dashboard&quot;.&#10;3 — WebApp attaches the JWT and calls the Looker API on GKE: PSC endpoint → Hub ILB → HA VPN tunnel (routes learned via BGP) → SPOKE 1 Tooling cluster.&#10;4 — Looker API FIRST calls ID&amp;A auth through the Apigee Internal Proxy (PSC), passing the JWT; ID&amp;A returns the result.&#10;5 — On OK, Looker API routes via the Reverse Proxy: 5a Spoke-1 DNS resolves the Looker FQDN via DNS peering to Hub DNS (which peers to Spoke-2&#39;s zone); 5b traffic goes Spoke-1 VPN → HUB, Hub Cloud Router re-advertises Spoke-2 routes (transit) → VPN → SPOKE 2 ILB → Looker pods.&#10;6 — Dashboard rendered back to the user. Login, auth and dashboard activity traced by Cloud Logging → Monitoring." style="text;html=1;fontSize=12;align=left;spacing=10;fillColor=#FFF3E0;strokeColor=#FB8C00;rounded=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="1420" width="2020" height="175" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root></mxGraphModel></diagram>
</mxfile>